---
<DocsLayout title="Server configuration" description="Configure thinDB listeners, memory, parallelism, files, authentication, and diagnostics." headings={headings}>
  <PageHeader eyebrow="Operate" title="Server configuration" description="The standalone server opens one shared catalog and exposes any combination of MySQL, PostgreSQL, and native listeners. Tune memory and worker limits to the machine, not to a cluster." />
  <h2 id="baseline">Production baseline</h2>
  <CodeBlock language="bash" code={`thindb-server \
  --data-dir /var/lib/thindb \
  --bind 10.0.10.15 \
  --mysql-port 3306 \
  --pg-port 5432 \
  --native-port 0 \
  --mysql-password "$THINDB_MYSQL_PASSWORD" \
  --pg-password "$THINDB_PG_PASSWORD" \
  --max-connections 256 \
  --idle-timeout-secs 1800 \
  --max-dop 8 \
  --memory-budget 16G \
  --query-memory-budget 4G \
  --cache-size 8G`} />
  <p>Pass bytes directly or use <code>K</code>, <code>M</code>, and <code>G</code> suffixes where supported. The data directory is created if absent.</p>

  <h2 id="config-file">Configuration file</h2>
  <p>Every flag can also be set in a flat <code>key = value</code> file passed with <code>--config PATH</code> (or the <code>THINDB_CONFIG</code> environment variable). Keys are the flag names without the leading <code>--</code>. This keeps a systemd unit or launch script small, and — because file values are read into memory rather than placed on the command line — it is the way to set a password that does <strong>not</strong> appear in <code>ps</code>.</p>
  <CodeBlock language="ini" code={`# /etc/thindb/thindb.conf
data-dir = /var/lib/thindb/data
bind = 0.0.0.0
mysql-port = 13310
pg-port = 0
native-port = 0
mysql-password = change-me       # read into memory, never in ps
cache-size = 12G
memory-budget = 8G
query-memory-budget = 4294967296 # raw bytes only (no suffix)
max-dop = 16
no-wal = false`} />
  <CodeBlock language="bash" code={`thindb-server --data-dir /var/lib/thindb --config /etc/thindb/thindb.conf`} />
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Precedence:</strong> a command-line flag overrides the same setting from the file, which overrides the built-in default (<code>CLI &gt; file &gt; default</code>).</li>
    <li><strong>Comments</strong> begin a line with <code>#</code>; inline comments are not supported, so a value may itself contain <code>#</code>. Wrap a value in quotes to preserve leading or trailing spaces.</li>
    <li><strong>Boolean toggles</strong> (<code>no-wal</code>, <code>no-compaction</code>) take <code>true</code>/<code>false</code> in the file.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="listeners-and-access">Listeners and access</h2>
  <div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Flag</th><th>Default</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td><code>--data-dir PATH</code></td><td>required</td><td>Catalog root and Zig-function persistence/build root.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>--bind ADDR</code></td><td><code>0.0.0.0</code></td><td>Bind interface shared by enabled listeners.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>--mysql-port PORT</code></td><td><code>3306</code></td><td>MySQL listener; <code>0</code> disables.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>--pg-port PORT</code></td><td><code>5432</code></td><td>PostgreSQL listener; <code>0</code> disables.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>--native-port PORT</code></td><td><code>7878</code></td><td>thinDB native listener; <code>0</code> disables.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>--mysql-password PW</code></td><td>trust</td><td>Require MySQL native-password authentication.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>--pg-password PW</code></td><td>trust</td><td>Require PostgreSQL SCRAM-SHA-256 authentication.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>--max-connections N</code></td><td><code>256</code></td><td>Process-wide cap across all wires.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>--idle-timeout-secs N</code></td><td><code>0</code></td><td>Close connections after read silence; zero disables.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>--file-root PATH</code></td><td>disabled</td><td>Allow SQL file scans only beneath this root.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>--xa-timeout-secs N</code></td><td><code>86400</code></td><td>Rollback stale prepared XA branches; zero disables.</td></tr>
  </tbody></table></div>
  <Callout type="warning" title="Secret handling"><p>Passing a password as a <em>flag</em> places it in process arguments, which local process-inspection tools can read. To keep a password out of <code>ps</code>, set <code>mysql-password</code> / <code>pg-password</code> in a <a href="#config-file">config file</a> (mode <code>600</code>) instead — file values are read into memory and never become command-line arguments.</p></Callout>

  <h2 id="memory">Memory budgets</h2>
  <div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Flag</th><th>Automatic behavior</th><th>Controls</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td><code>--query-memory-budget B</code></td><td>Approximately 25% of physical RAM, floor 256 MiB.</td><td>One query's blocking operators.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>--memory-budget B</code></td><td>Approximately 50% of physical RAM, floor 256 MiB.</td><td>Shared reservations across concurrent queries.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>--cache-size B</code></td><td>Current engine auto-sizing uses approximately 35% of RAM, floor 256 MiB.</td><td>One global decompressed block buffer pool shared by every table.</td></tr>
  </tbody></table></div>
  <p>Sorts, hash group-by, hash-join build sides, sort-merge buffers, and materialization reserve query memory. The decompressed block cache is a separate bucket. A tracked budget of <code>0</code> disables that tracker.</p>
  <Callout type="warning" title="No spill"><p>Blocking operators do not spill to disk. A query that cannot fit its estimated or actual budget fails with <code>MemoryBudgetExceeded</code> instead of silently degrading.</p></Callout>

  <h2 id="parallelism-and-compaction">Parallelism and compaction</h2>
  <div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Flag</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td><code>--max-dop N</code></td><td>Maximum scan/filter workers per query, further limited by a shared worker-slot budget.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>--compact-threads N</code></td><td>Threads used for block encode/compress during compaction; zero selects about 25% of physical cores.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>--no-compaction</code></td><td>Disables the background compactor. Use only as an operational escape hatch; segment count will grow.</td></tr>
  </tbody></table></div>

  <h2 id="diagnostics">Diagnostics</h2>
  <ul><li><code>--profile-ops</code> prints inclusive per-operator timings after each query.</li><li><code>--trace-group-by</code> prints hash/sort/radix routing inputs and decisions.</li><li><code>--force-group-by auto|hash|sort|radix</code> overrides routing for diagnosis and benchmarks.</li><li><code>THINDB_MYSQL_PROFILE=1</code> logs per-connection MySQL protocol phase timings.</li><li><code>--scan-batch N</code> overrides the scan sub-batch size for diagnostics.</li><li><code>--version</code> and <code>--help</code> report the binary build and current flags.</li></ul>
  <Callout type="note" title="Diagnostic overrides"><p>Forced group-by and scan-batch settings are process-wide diagnostic controls. Do not use benchmark overrides as unexplained production defaults.</p></Callout>
  <PageLinks previous={{ label: 'Embedded UDFs', href: '/functions/embedded/' }} next={{ label: 'Storage and durability', href: '/operations/storage/' }} />
</DocsLayout>
